{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully enacted the S-list-project with 57 real Pennsylvania cities, and the persona creation for \"Wendell\" is coherent. However, the chat invocation is puzzling: while a response was generated with sequential respondents and a speech floor, the chat matched zero tool needs, indicated by empty `intents` and `needIds` fields. This contradicts the scenario's requirement for matching tool needs, even though a response `needId` was created and processed."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:27.181870100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe S-competing-tools mechanism is now more general, evidenced by compare.py running over all `need:` tools and a two-adequate competitor scenario in set-build. While the S-competing-tools demo itself still shows one working versus one unconfigured tool, the underlying machinery is proven. S-defer-publication also correctly handled both no-grant and with-grant cases, indicating real behavior."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:29.469373+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe S-exchange-import scenario failed unexpectedly, with an import error stating \"not a meridian.exchange/v1 package\" even though the system just exported the package. This suggests a potential regression or a harness bug, possibly related to importing the wrong path or a format mismatch where self-exported packages cannot be re-imported. This failure significantly lowers the scenario's score, likely to 0.3-0.4, despite the underlying import mechanics existing in the code. Other scenarios, S-focused-need, S-assertion-input, and S-template-need, ran with varying degrees of success and thin enactments, scoring between 0.3 and 0.8."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:32.875697600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe candidate ranking favors the hardcover version (0.9 confidence) over the PDF (0.4 confidence), which aligns with the D3 contextual ranking, though it seems to retain failed evidence. The overall confidence is thin but adequate at approximately 0.75."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:34.188375+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm seeing an inconsistency between the `S-background-present` data and the archive evidence regarding temporal attention findings. While `S-background-present.json` shows empty findings and zero context count for temporal attention, the archive evidence indicates a persona (\"Stewardship pass — temporal attention\") presented actual findings, like an \"atlas study check-in\" and project linkage. This suggests `S-background-present` might have captured an earlier or incorrect row, or the steward spoke findings but logged an empty context row. Nevertheless, D6 is enacted because the persona response with findings is archived, earning a score of approximately 0.8."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:34.847323700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've enacted S-restart-recovery, and it seems to have worked, but I'm flagging a potential bug in _temporal: a \"recent\" event is dated 2030, which is odd. Ethics-gate-F1 is implemented, though a liveness lookup failed for the refusal test, which I handled. Connectors-F8 is also enacted, but the RSS feed is available but unevidenced, and a verification file is missing. Archive-C-ConversationArchive is enacted and appears real. I'll now check launch logs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:33:37.135831300+00:00"}}}}
