{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've confirmed the new modules are functional, with `ethics.py` performing Wikipedia liveness checks and handling refusals, `speechfloor.py` acting as a FIFO thread, `connectors.py` making HTTP requests, and `temporal.py` managing context. `personas.py` integrates these into a minting process with refusals and permanent marks. The S-list project evidence is solid, showing the correct 57 PA cities with live timings and disagreements. I'm now verifying the iterative nature of the `need:` arc for the S-list project. The \"imitates Barack Obama\" mint's ethics gate seems fast; the 77ms lookup for `imitationMint: ok` is suspicious given the 404 on a refused mint's lookup, suggesting the wiki path was indeed exercised. The refused mint's `liveness` verdict of \"unclear\" with `reachable:false` and an `objection match` correctly resulted in a refusal."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:34:33.624256+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-21T06:34:34.183438Z  INFO connect_post{path="/exa.product_analytics_pb.ProductAnalyticsService/BatchRecordAnalyticsEvents"}: connect_rpc::client: close time.busy=134µs time.idle=97.9ms
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm scoring the launch based on several criteria: probe success, launch stability, and recovery logs, yielding a 0.9 score with 0.85 confidence. Existing features are mostly covered, with improvements in connectors, ethics, persona art, and voice diversity, though several key areas like fleet, exchange media, and advanced STT remain absent, resulting in a 0.55 score and 0.7 confidence. Completeness is high at 0.85, with most required behaviors delivered except for a driver bug impacting import and thin spoken-input depth. Fleet and exchange media installations are correctly reported as absent, with high confidence."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:34:35.724017300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"tree-fire","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm recalculating the overall score, which is the mean of the five scored criteria. The previous rescoring used a formula that resulted in 0.42, but the current calculation yields 0.46. I've decided to keep the overall score as the mean of these five criteria, excluding the user score and scenario suite from the average. Most scenarios scored well, except for S-exchange-import, which failed due to a driver bug, though the underlying machinery was verified."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:34:37.512897+00:00"}}}}
